# What evidence a change must produce before finishup will land it.
#
# fast-path      a change touching only these needs no full CI suite
# standard-check must be present and SUCCESS on the PR head for everything else
#
# Fast is earned by the diff, never requested: one path outside this list and
# the whole PR is standard.
#
# NOTE: the four CI jobs below carry a display `name:` with spaces
# ("Lint & typecheck", etc). ci-autoland's own .ci-policy parser
# (Repo.policy() in scripts/ci-autoland/autoland.py) splits each line on
# whitespace and takes only the token immediately after `standard-check`, so
# it cannot match a multi-word check name today — `required()` would end up
# looking for a check literally named "Lint" and never see it go green. This
# is written with the real check names anyway, since that's what actually
# appears on the PR; the parser needs a fix (join the remaining tokens) or
# the four jobs need single-word names before ci-autoland can land PRs here.

fast-path      docs/**
fast-path      *.md

# PRs that are not drafts land on green through ci-autoland (~/Automation).
autoland

standard-check Lint & typecheck
standard-check Unit & integration (Vitest + jest-expo)
standard-check Cross-service e2e
standard-check Agent config drift
